From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: skip transparent proxy without netns capability

Being uid 0 in a container does not imply CAP_SYS_ADMIN. Probe the exact
network-namespace operation required by the transparent proxy integration
test and report the Automake skip status when the sandbox forbids it. The
test still runs unchanged on capable hosts.

Patch-Source: openEuler RISC-V package CI failure analysis
Patch-License: BSD-2-Clause
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes are not authorized)
---
 tests/transparent_proxy_test | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/transparent_proxy_test b/tests/transparent_proxy_test
--- a/tests/transparent_proxy_test
+++ b/tests/transparent_proxy_test
@@ -87,6 +87,13 @@ sub main {
         exit 77;
     }
 
+    my $probe_namespace = "ns-sniproxy-capability-$$";
+    if (system('ip', 'netns', 'add', $probe_namespace) != 0) {
+        print STDERR "This test requires network namespace capabilities\n";
+        exit 77;
+    }
+    checked_system('ip', 'netns', 'del', $probe_namespace);
+
     # Setup a test network using network namespaces with the ns-test-proxy
     # namespace configured like a normal transparent proxy box.
     #
-- 
